{"audio": "james-04.opus", "duration_ms": 132892, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2100, "end_ms": 3260, "text": "James, Chapter Four."}, {"start_ms": 4540, "end_ms": 6901, "text": "What causes conflicts and quarrels among you?"}, {"start_ms": 7341, "end_ms": 9781, "text": "Don’t they come from the passions at war within you?"}, {"start_ms": 10541, "end_ms": 15361, "text": "You crave what you do not have; you kill and covet, but are unable to obtain it."}, {"start_ms": 15821, "end_ms": 16882, "text": "You quarrel and fight."}, {"start_ms": 17282, "end_ms": 19702, "text": "You do not have, because you do not ask."}, {"start_ms": 20302, "end_ms": 26522, "text": "And when you do ask, you do not receive, because you ask with wrong motives, that you may squander it on your pleasures."}, {"start_ms": 27582, "end_ms": 28623, "text": "You adulteresses!"}, {"start_ms": 29103, "end_ms": 32903, "text": "Do you not know that friendship with the world is hostility toward God?"}, {"start_ms": 33683, "end_ms": 38824, "text": "Therefore, whoever chooses to be a friend of the world renders himself an enemy of God."}, {"start_ms": 39624, "end_ms": 45564, "text": "Or do you think the Scripture says without reason that the Spirit He caused to dwell in us yearns with envy?"}, {"start_ms": 46164, "end_ms": 47604, "text": "But He gives us more grace."}, {"start_ms": 48084, "end_ms": 55885, "text": "This is why it says: “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.” Submit yourselves, then, to God."}, {"start_ms": 56305, "end_ms": 58325, "text": "Resist the devil, and he will flee from you."}, {"start_ms": 58765, "end_ms": 61266, "text": "Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you."}, {"start_ms": 61886, "end_ms": 65666, "text": "Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you double-minded."}, {"start_ms": 66286, "end_ms": 68046, "text": "Grieve, mourn, and weep."}, {"start_ms": 68746, "end_ms": 71506, "text": "Turn your laughter to mourning, and your joy to gloom."}, {"start_ms": 72247, "end_ms": 75267, "text": "Humble yourselves before the Lord, and He will exalt you."}, {"start_ms": 76347, "end_ms": 78327, "text": "Brothers, do not slander one another."}, {"start_ms": 78827, "end_ms": 84068, "text": "Anyone who speaks against his brother or judges him speaks against the law and judges it."}, {"start_ms": 84648, "end_ms": 88708, "text": "And if you judge the law, you are not a practitioner of the law, but a judge of it."}, {"start_ms": 89568, "end_ms": 94209, "text": "There is only one Lawgiver and Judge, the One who is able to save and destroy."}, {"start_ms": 94789, "end_ms": 96609, "text": "But who are you to judge your neighbor?"}, {"start_ms": 97989, "end_ms": 108910, "text": "Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go to this or that city, spend a year there, carry on business, and make a profit.” You do not even know what will happen tomorrow!"}, {"start_ms": 109630, "end_ms": 110390, "text": "What is your life?"}, {"start_ms": 110930, "end_ms": 114530, "text": "You are a mist that appears for a little while and then vanishes."}, {"start_ms": 115550, "end_ms": 123111, "text": "Instead, you ought to say, “If the Lord is willing, we will live and do this or that.” As it is, you boast in your proud intentions."}, {"start_ms": 123831, "end_ms": 125571, "text": "All such boasting is evil."}, {"start_ms": 126431, "end_ms": 131332, "text": "Anyone, then, who knows the right thing to do, yet fails to do it, is guilty of sin."}], "words": [{"t": "James,", "s": 2100, "e": 2520, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2620, "e": 2940, "si": 0}, {"t": "Four.", "s": 3000, "e": 3260, "si": 0}, {"t": "What", "s": 4540, "e": 4720, "si": 1}, {"t": "causes", "s": 4780, "e": 5220, "si": 1}, {"t": "conflicts", "s": 5300, "e": 5841, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 5881, "e": 6001, "si": 1}, {"t": "quarrels", "s": 6061, "e": 6481, "si": 1}, {"t": "among", "s": 6541, "e": 6761, "si": 1}, {"t": "you?", "s": 6801, "e": 6901, "si": 1}, {"t": "Don’t